1
00:00:05,516 --> 00:00:08,180
You have been charged with embezzling funds.

2
00:00:08,190 --> 00:00:09,820
Dad! Grandma!

3
00:00:10,300 --> 00:00:11,301
Phob, thank you

4
00:00:12,028 --> 00:00:13,060
for everything.

5
00:00:15,564 --> 00:00:17,565
I'll be looking forward to seeing you succeed.

6
00:00:22,402 --> 00:00:23,820
Is selling this palace

7
00:00:24,199 --> 00:00:26,020
really our only option?

8
00:00:26,871 --> 00:00:29,564
Your Highness, I wish you have a better life.

9
00:00:34,820 --> 00:00:37,180
Sometimes I can't help but wonder...

10
00:00:37,436 --> 00:00:39,260
was everything I lost

11
00:00:39,618 --> 00:00:40,940
really worth it?

12
00:00:41,372 --> 00:00:42,500
I am rooting for you.

13
00:02:15,225 --> 00:02:16,226
Look at this.

14
00:02:20,892 --> 00:02:22,735
The government has ordered another review of the press.

15
00:02:23,159 --> 00:02:25,516
Any newspaper that criticizes the government too harshly

16
00:02:25,959 --> 00:02:27,204
gets summoned or shut down.

17
00:02:27,898 --> 00:02:30,660
Things are even more restrictive now than they were before the revolution.

18
00:02:30,660 --> 00:02:35,332
We fought to change this country

19
00:02:35,759 --> 00:02:37,940
because we wanted people to have rights and freedoms.

20
00:02:38,383 --> 00:02:40,372
So tell me—how is this any different from what came before?

21
00:02:48,884 --> 00:02:49,885
It does make a difference.

22
00:02:58,292 --> 00:02:59,556
I’ve asked myself the same thing—

23
00:03:02,543 --> 00:03:03,544
whether what we did

24
00:03:03,730 --> 00:03:06,202
really changed anything at all.

25
00:03:10,362 --> 00:03:12,116
But someone once told me that

26
00:03:14,815 --> 00:03:15,816
we may not see the difference

27
00:03:17,898 --> 00:03:19,791
we’ve made in the grand scheme of things.

28
00:03:21,050 --> 00:03:22,127
But in the lives of ordinary people,

29
00:03:23,316 --> 00:03:24,317
we’ve already made a difference.

30
00:03:29,426 --> 00:03:30,427
Maybe

31
00:03:31,756 --> 00:03:32,962
what we do

32
00:03:34,215 --> 00:03:36,391
can’t change the whole world overnight.

33
00:03:37,343 --> 00:03:38,344
But at least

34
00:03:39,052 --> 00:03:40,610
it can change someone’s life

35
00:03:41,698 --> 00:03:42,799
and give them hope.

36
00:03:49,916 --> 00:03:51,460
Are you talking about Prince Tinnakorn?

37
00:03:55,890 --> 00:03:57,100
It is that obvious?

38
00:03:59,636 --> 00:04:01,380
Ever since you came back from the school that day,

39
00:04:02,687 --> 00:04:04,700
you’ve seemed more like yourself again.

40
00:04:09,690 --> 00:04:10,980
Before I went to see him that day,

41
00:04:13,391 --> 00:04:16,860
I’d planned out everything I wanted to say.

42
00:04:18,447 --> 00:04:19,740
I wanted to tell him

43
00:04:21,028 --> 00:04:22,300
how deeply sorry I was.

44
00:04:25,402 --> 00:04:28,820
I wanted to beg him to let us go back to the way we were.

45
00:04:30,570 --> 00:04:31,620
But when the moment came,

46
00:04:33,060 --> 00:04:34,220
I couldn’t say a word.

47
00:04:38,618 --> 00:04:40,780
He seemed so much stronger than I was.

48
00:04:44,412 --> 00:04:45,940
What are you going to do?

49
00:04:47,959 --> 00:04:48,980
I don’t know.

50
00:04:51,948 --> 00:04:54,049
I’m not hoping for things

51
00:04:54,530 --> 00:04:55,767
to go back to the way they were.

52
00:04:57,767 --> 00:04:58,868
But if I ever get the chance,

53
00:05:01,548 --> 00:05:04,820
I hope he’ll open up to me again, even just a little.

54
00:05:07,628 --> 00:05:09,440
I still want to walk beside him,

55
00:05:11,919 --> 00:05:13,420
and I never want to hurt him again.

56
00:05:19,439 --> 00:05:20,708
I once chose my belief

57
00:05:23,524 --> 00:05:25,791
over the person I loved most, and I ended up hurting him.

58
00:05:27,642 --> 00:05:28,643
From now on,

59
00:05:30,986 --> 00:05:32,220
if I’m given another chance,

60
00:05:35,458 --> 00:05:37,060
I want to make him proud

61
00:05:40,188 --> 00:05:41,700
instead of causing him more pain.

62
00:05:59,314 --> 00:06:00,940
What are you planting?

63
00:06:04,287 --> 00:06:07,519
Oh, it's cotton rose tree. Where did you get it?

64
00:06:08,176 --> 00:06:10,964
The principal planted several of them at school,

65
00:06:11,578 --> 00:06:13,780
so I asked if I could have one to plant here at home.

66
00:06:18,138 --> 00:06:19,740
You miss him, don't you?

67
00:06:27,159 --> 00:06:28,876
Trees are remarkable, aren’t they?

68
00:06:29,506 --> 00:06:31,420
No matter where they’re transplanted,

69
00:06:31,687 --> 00:06:34,220
as long as their roots remain strong,

70
00:06:35,047 --> 00:06:38,500
they’ll grow again before long.

71
00:06:40,511 --> 00:06:42,380
Perhaps trees are luckier than people.

72
00:06:44,087 --> 00:06:46,855
Give them soil and water, and they can grow again.

73
00:06:48,876 --> 00:06:50,260
But people are different.

74
00:06:51,527 --> 00:06:53,860
No matter how much we may wish to go back to the way things were,

75
00:06:55,031 --> 00:06:56,300
some things can never be the same again.

76
00:07:02,551 --> 00:07:04,898
Who says things have to be the same?

77
00:07:05,532 --> 00:07:09,148
People are strange, aren’t they?

78
00:07:09,410 --> 00:07:12,039
Why do we always think our lives, our happiness,

79
00:07:12,076 --> 00:07:14,780
have to stay the same forever?

80
00:07:15,850 --> 00:07:20,040
Take the things we own, for example. When something gets broken

81
00:07:20,340 --> 00:07:21,341
or damaged,

82
00:07:21,908 --> 00:07:24,940
it may never work the way it used to.

83
00:07:25,394 --> 00:07:28,295
But that doesn’t mean it can’t still be good.

84
00:07:30,951 --> 00:07:31,952
Grandma?

85
00:07:35,831 --> 00:07:38,300
I want to tell you about life.

86
00:07:38,754 --> 00:07:42,498
Life isn’t about trying to hold on to the same happiness

87
00:07:42,972 --> 00:07:45,860
and success forever.

88
00:07:47,436 --> 00:07:51,303
Listen to me. What matters most is learning…

89
00:07:52,194 --> 00:07:53,700
to accept

90
00:07:54,700 --> 00:07:56,063
and understand

91
00:07:56,772 --> 00:07:58,874
the things that change,

92
00:07:59,951 --> 00:08:01,300
to live with those changes…

93
00:08:02,692 --> 00:08:04,029
with grace,

94
00:08:05,082 --> 00:08:06,860
and to make the best of what we have.

95
00:08:07,930 --> 00:08:08,931
Okay?

96
00:08:09,679 --> 00:08:10,680
Okay.

97
00:08:17,636 --> 00:08:19,340
Thank you so much.

98
00:08:27,122 --> 00:08:28,380
Grandma! Grandma!

99
00:08:30,241 --> 00:08:31,742
- Grandma?
- Your Highness?

100
00:08:32,114 --> 00:08:33,700
Let's get her inside. Grandma?

101
00:08:38,242 --> 00:08:40,764
Grandma, maybe we should go to the hospital.

102
00:08:41,111 --> 00:08:42,620
Oh, I don't have to.

103
00:08:43,052 --> 00:08:46,540
That’s just what happens when you get old. You get a little dizzy now and then.

104
00:08:46,692 --> 00:08:48,740
I’ll be fine after a bit of rest.

105
00:08:49,103 --> 00:08:50,980
But you don't look fine to me.

106
00:08:52,186 --> 00:08:55,740
Should I contact Chat and Dad?

107
00:08:56,620 --> 00:08:58,060
No need to.

108
00:08:58,242 --> 00:09:00,711
We don't have to trouble them.

109
00:09:01,127 --> 00:09:04,567
They already have a lot on their plates.

110
00:09:06,519 --> 00:09:07,520
Grandma?

111
00:09:08,300 --> 00:09:11,068
Oh, I know why I got lightheaded.

112
00:09:11,442 --> 00:09:13,170
I must be hungry.

113
00:09:13,639 --> 00:09:15,540
The desserts sold so well today

114
00:09:15,650 --> 00:09:17,802
that I got busy and forgot to eat.

115
00:09:18,474 --> 00:09:21,951
I knew it! You had me so worried.

116
00:09:22,106 --> 00:09:23,700
That’s why I told you

117
00:09:23,892 --> 00:09:26,180
to stop and get something to eat at the market first.

118
00:09:26,420 --> 00:09:28,970
You’d better watch yourself, Aum!

119
00:09:29,519 --> 00:09:33,220
Stop talking and finding me something to eat.

120
00:09:34,351 --> 00:09:35,660
- Sure.
- I'm starving.

121
00:09:36,938 --> 00:09:41,051
The desserts were selling so well today that I got too busy to eat.

122
00:09:41,252 --> 00:09:43,540
Let me lie down for a bit. I’ll be fine.

123
00:09:44,060 --> 00:09:47,020
Then I’ll go prepare some herbal medicine for you.

124
00:09:48,740 --> 00:09:50,186
- I'll be right back.
- Okay.

125
00:10:13,220 --> 00:10:15,221
No! No!

126
00:10:17,300 --> 00:10:18,740
The forces that will join us…

127
00:10:19,100 --> 00:10:20,990
are from Ubon Ratchathani, Nakhon Sawan,

128
00:10:21,252 --> 00:10:23,660
Prachin Buri, Ratchaburi, and Phetchaburi.

129
00:10:24,282 --> 00:10:25,972
But I still have my doubts.

130
00:10:26,377 --> 00:10:29,108
We don’t know whether the units that pledged their support will actually join us.

131
00:10:29,428 --> 00:10:31,226
Many of them are reluctant to fight their own countrymen.

132
00:10:31,640 --> 00:10:32,660
Their own side?

133
00:10:34,178 --> 00:10:35,700
Ever since they seized power, they’ve driven our people…

134
00:10:36,300 --> 00:10:39,468
out of government service and imprisoned members of the royal family.

135
00:10:40,556 --> 00:10:42,840
They turned those who had served this country their entire lives

136
00:10:42,860 --> 00:10:44,239
into enemies of the state.

137
00:10:47,306 --> 00:10:49,706
They stopped seeing us as their own a long time ago.

138
00:10:51,397 --> 00:10:53,220
Today they silence the press.

139
00:10:53,819 --> 00:10:55,700
Tomorrow, they’ll silence anyone who disagrees with them.

140
00:10:56,298 --> 00:10:57,823
And one day, what will be left of Siam?

141
00:11:00,111 --> 00:11:02,620
I will not stand by and watch Siam

142
00:11:02,822 --> 00:11:04,570
be led down the wrong path.

143
00:11:04,991 --> 00:11:06,340
I agree with you, Your Highness.

144
00:11:06,810 --> 00:11:08,634
Even if they brand me a traitor, so be it.

145
00:11:09,044 --> 00:11:10,540
This is no rebellion.

146
00:11:11,636 --> 00:11:13,740
We are fighting to reclaim our country.

147
00:11:14,754 --> 00:11:16,586
If we do not rise up today,

148
00:11:17,036 --> 00:11:19,790
there may be no country left for us to defend tomorrow.

149
00:11:30,220 --> 00:11:33,940
Why are you setting up the shop yourself? Where is Aum?

150
00:11:34,120 --> 00:11:37,660
Oh, I asked Aum to buy food for me. I'm quite hungry.

151
00:11:39,695 --> 00:11:40,940
I'll leave you to it.

152
00:11:43,871 --> 00:11:45,663
Khanom Jeen is here.

153
00:11:46,964 --> 00:11:48,460
They look so good.

154
00:11:49,352 --> 00:11:52,302
We have steamed banana cakes and coconut-filled sweets today.

155
00:11:52,353 --> 00:11:54,580
- Which one do you want?
- I'll take three of these.

156
00:11:54,748 --> 00:11:56,940
One bag of this one, this one…and that one.

157
00:11:58,562 --> 00:12:00,140
- I'll put them in the bags for you.
- Let me check on chicken.

158
00:12:00,220 --> 00:12:01,260
- Sure.
- Okay.

159
00:12:04,452 --> 00:12:06,060
Your Highness!

160
00:12:08,519 --> 00:12:09,520
Your Highness!

161
00:12:09,898 --> 00:12:12,020
Please help! She passed out!

162
00:12:15,964 --> 00:12:17,860
She passed out! Please help!

163
00:12:19,512 --> 00:12:20,700
- Princess.
- She passed out, sir.

164
00:12:21,431 --> 00:12:22,432
Let me help you get her up.

165
00:12:23,351 --> 00:12:24,352
Your Highness!

166
00:12:26,460 --> 00:12:27,461
Easy there.

167
00:12:32,660 --> 00:12:34,661
[Siamvejsathan Hospital]

168
00:12:35,500 --> 00:12:37,501
[Emergency Room]

169
00:12:50,995 --> 00:12:51,996
How is my grandma?

170
00:12:53,309 --> 00:12:54,580
The doctor hasn't come out yet.

171
00:12:55,679 --> 00:12:56,680
Where is Aum?

172
00:12:57,279 --> 00:12:58,900
She's in the room with Princess Patthamapriya.

173
00:13:02,080 --> 00:13:04,380
How did this happen? She was fine this morning.

174
00:13:05,180 --> 00:13:06,380
Please calm down.

175
00:13:07,181 --> 00:13:08,620
Your grandma will be okay.

176
00:13:16,719 --> 00:13:18,543
- Has the patient's family been here yet?
- I'm here.

177
00:13:19,220 --> 00:13:20,860
The doctor would like to see you. This way, please.

178
00:13:31,314 --> 00:13:34,100
She is now suffering from kidney failure.

179
00:13:34,740 --> 00:13:36,540
Toxins are building up in her blood,

180
00:13:36,996 --> 00:13:39,060
and her electrolytes are severely imbalanced.

181
00:13:39,634 --> 00:13:41,860
At this point, all we can do is provide supportive care.

182
00:13:42,335 --> 00:13:46,020
The rest depends on how her body responds.

183
00:13:46,364 --> 00:13:47,620
What do you mean?

184
00:13:48,722 --> 00:13:50,260
Will she recover soon?

185
00:13:50,940 --> 00:13:52,980
- For how long?
- Aum.

186
00:13:54,041 --> 00:13:56,100
Stop yelling already.

187
00:13:56,540 --> 00:13:59,180
You’re always embarrassing me.

188
00:14:00,060 --> 00:14:01,980
Well, I am worried about you, Your Highness.

189
00:14:02,540 --> 00:14:05,260
I heard the doctor but I didn't get it.

190
00:14:07,143 --> 00:14:08,620
Did you get it, Phob?

191
00:14:15,746 --> 00:14:17,060
It's okay, Grandma.

192
00:14:17,687 --> 00:14:20,220
The doctor will heal you, you will get better soon.

193
00:14:34,516 --> 00:14:35,660
Please be careful.

194
00:14:38,223 --> 00:14:39,224
Walk slowly.

195
00:14:40,628 --> 00:14:41,629
Have a seat, please.

196
00:14:50,087 --> 00:14:53,116
Auntie, please find something for her to eat.

197
00:14:53,383 --> 00:14:55,085
- So she can take her medicine.
- Okay.

198
00:14:55,314 --> 00:14:58,540
She needs to take the medicine the doctor prescribed on time.

199
00:14:59,340 --> 00:15:01,120
The doctor will see her again in two weeks.

200
00:15:01,440 --> 00:15:02,460
I will come and take her to the hospital.

201
00:15:02,610 --> 00:15:04,620
Oh, you don't have to.

202
00:15:05,015 --> 00:15:07,060
I can take her, I don't want to bother you.

203
00:15:07,364 --> 00:15:08,860
You won't be bothering me.

204
00:15:09,752 --> 00:15:10,940
Please let me take her to the hospital.

205
00:15:11,660 --> 00:15:13,100
But I think I should--

206
00:15:13,261 --> 00:15:15,460
Thank you so much, Phob.

207
00:16:17,794 --> 00:16:18,795
Phob.

208
00:16:26,511 --> 00:16:29,780
This is for the medicine and the doctor’s fee today.

209
00:16:30,319 --> 00:16:31,780
Thank you for today. Here, please take it.

210
00:16:36,666 --> 00:16:38,540
I don't think I can take it.

211
00:16:39,330 --> 00:16:40,331
You should take it.

212
00:16:41,300 --> 00:16:45,220
You’ve already done more than enough just by taking her to the doctor.

213
00:16:45,764 --> 00:16:46,780
It’s no trouble at all, Your Highness.

214
00:16:48,247 --> 00:16:51,340
I owe her more than I could ever repay.

215
00:16:53,906 --> 00:16:57,460
This is the least I can do.

216
00:17:05,772 --> 00:17:06,773
Thank you.

217
00:17:16,367 --> 00:17:18,120
Are you okay, Your Highness?

218
00:17:26,356 --> 00:17:27,357
I'm scared.

219
00:17:28,953 --> 00:17:30,700
I'm scared I'm gonna lose my grandma.

220
00:17:32,727 --> 00:17:34,580
I should have noticed her symptoms sooner.

221
00:17:35,340 --> 00:17:38,380
So I could take her to the hospital, to see the doctor.

222
00:17:40,754 --> 00:17:42,180
Why can't I do anything?

223
00:17:42,423 --> 00:17:43,780
I couldn't save anyone.

224
00:17:45,540 --> 00:17:47,620
I'm scared that I will be left alone.

225
00:17:51,680 --> 00:17:53,240
What if I have to be alone?

226
00:17:57,826 --> 00:17:58,827
Phob?

227
00:18:24,770 --> 00:18:25,780
It's okay, Your Highness.

228
00:18:29,767 --> 00:18:30,860
Your Phob is here for you.

229
00:18:44,135 --> 00:18:45,136
Phob.

230
00:18:47,868 --> 00:18:48,980
Morning, dear.

231
00:18:50,108 --> 00:18:51,109
Let me help you.

232
00:19:25,932 --> 00:19:27,933
[Pharmacy]

233
00:19:37,738 --> 00:19:40,780
Take one tablet three times a day—morning, noon, and evening,

234
00:19:43,142 --> 00:19:44,143
This one is to be taken after meals.

235
00:19:44,620 --> 00:19:45,900
Ew, it's so bitter.

236
00:19:47,703 --> 00:19:49,180
This is a good stuff, Your Highness.

237
00:19:49,431 --> 00:19:50,740
Then you eat it.

238
00:19:54,340 --> 00:19:55,541
It's too bitter.

239
00:19:57,060 --> 00:20:00,220
Have some candied jujube to take away the bitter taste, Your Highness.

240
00:20:01,292 --> 00:20:03,380
Thank you, Phob.

241
00:20:08,586 --> 00:20:09,660
Oh, it's better.

242
00:20:23,660 --> 00:20:25,236
Phob, the cotton rose we planted has finally bloomed.

243
00:21:41,140 --> 00:21:42,463
Please be careful.

244
00:21:45,570 --> 00:21:47,220
Please slow down.

245
00:21:48,604 --> 00:21:51,860
I’m going to trip and fall because of you!

246
00:21:51,986 --> 00:21:55,740
You keep darting back and forth in front of me. So annoying.

247
00:21:56,056 --> 00:21:58,060
It’s slippery here, Your Highness. Please be careful.

248
00:21:58,994 --> 00:22:00,340
Just leave me alone.

249
00:22:00,546 --> 00:22:01,780
Please be careful.

250
00:22:19,847 --> 00:22:20,900
Phob?

251
00:22:24,724 --> 00:22:26,660
What brings you here?

252
00:22:27,567 --> 00:22:30,568
It’s not time for my checkup yet, is it?

253
00:22:33,146 --> 00:22:34,660
Someone is here to see you, Your Highness.

254
00:22:36,240 --> 00:22:37,241
Who?

255
00:22:58,527 --> 00:22:59,528
Nual?

256
00:23:07,394 --> 00:23:10,100
Oh, Nual. Get up.

257
00:23:12,395 --> 00:23:13,860
It's you. It really is you.

258
00:23:18,482 --> 00:23:19,783
I missed you.

259
00:23:21,922 --> 00:23:22,923
I missed you.

260
00:23:38,215 --> 00:23:40,300
You shouldn’t have to live like this.

261
00:23:41,388 --> 00:23:42,389
This is all

262
00:23:43,740 --> 00:23:44,741
because of Phob.

263
00:23:48,252 --> 00:23:51,425
Look at what you’ve done!

264
00:23:52,660 --> 00:23:54,730
She used to live in comfort,

265
00:23:55,359 --> 00:23:56,360
and now look at her...

266
00:23:56,370 --> 00:23:58,620
It's okay. Don't yell at him.

267
00:23:59,412 --> 00:24:02,260
Phob, why don’t you help Aum put things away?

268
00:24:02,647 --> 00:24:05,120
You bought so many things.

269
00:24:14,434 --> 00:24:17,220
Nual, come sit up here with me.

270
00:24:19,644 --> 00:24:20,940
It wouldn’t be proper, Your Highness.

271
00:24:21,645 --> 00:24:23,060
Oh, it’s all right.

272
00:24:23,338 --> 00:24:26,521
There’s no such thing as proper or improper anymore.

273
00:24:26,666 --> 00:24:28,420
Come here.

274
00:24:28,490 --> 00:24:31,700
Come sit with me. Make yourself comfortable.

275
00:24:33,263 --> 00:24:34,360
Come on.

276
00:24:49,060 --> 00:24:50,061
I…

277
00:24:51,556 --> 00:24:53,190
I failed as a mother.

278
00:24:54,695 --> 00:24:56,820
If I’d raised him better,

279
00:25:00,956 --> 00:25:03,660
none of this would’ve happened, Your Highness.

280
00:25:03,680 --> 00:25:06,660
Stop it, don't blame him.

281
00:25:08,031 --> 00:25:09,032
Your Highness.

282
00:25:10,292 --> 00:25:12,133
Aren’t you angry at Phob for what he did?

283
00:25:12,860 --> 00:25:13,861
Of course I’m angry.

284
00:25:14,861 --> 00:25:18,260
And I’m deeply hurt.

285
00:25:19,191 --> 00:25:22,100
But what’s happening now goes

286
00:25:22,812 --> 00:25:25,220
far beyond Phob.

287
00:25:26,340 --> 00:25:28,040
Even if he had never been involved,

288
00:25:28,906 --> 00:25:30,341
sooner or later,

289
00:25:30,927 --> 00:25:33,400
something like this would have happened anyway.

290
00:25:33,466 --> 00:25:35,620
But Phob still shouldn’t have...

291
00:25:36,610 --> 00:25:38,620
shouldn’t have sided with those people.

292
00:25:40,316 --> 00:25:43,100
He should’ve remembered everything your family had done for him.

293
00:25:43,250 --> 00:25:45,260
He does.

294
00:25:46,066 --> 00:25:50,500
If he didn’t, he wouldn’t be suffering this much.

295
00:25:51,938 --> 00:25:53,500
But we have to understand

296
00:25:54,306 --> 00:25:56,980
that young people today

297
00:25:57,383 --> 00:25:59,380
see life differently from our generation.

298
00:26:00,156 --> 00:26:01,700
We look to the past,

299
00:26:02,991 --> 00:26:04,980
while they look to the future.

300
00:26:05,372 --> 00:26:07,580
They don’t see things

301
00:26:08,460 --> 00:26:10,300
in terms of who was right or wrong.

302
00:26:11,010 --> 00:26:12,140
All they know

303
00:26:12,996 --> 00:26:16,180
is that they’re willing to sacrifice everything

304
00:26:16,428 --> 00:26:20,340
for what they believe in.

305
00:26:23,106 --> 00:26:24,620
And perhaps,

306
00:26:25,279 --> 00:26:27,020
in the end,

307
00:26:28,220 --> 00:26:30,900
it’s we who have to learn to let go.

308
00:26:36,031 --> 00:26:37,032
Nual,

309
00:26:37,732 --> 00:26:40,020
the same goes for you.

310
00:26:40,617 --> 00:26:42,660
You need to learn to let go, too,

311
00:26:43,194 --> 00:26:44,940
of everything

312
00:26:45,383 --> 00:26:47,580
that’s happening now,

313
00:26:47,879 --> 00:26:49,340
and even what happened

314
00:26:51,735 --> 00:26:54,060
between Phob and Tin.

315
00:26:57,391 --> 00:26:58,392
Your Highness?

316
00:27:00,036 --> 00:27:02,180
You knew about this?

317
00:27:04,196 --> 00:27:05,297
You must have known

318
00:27:06,076 --> 00:27:09,380
about this for a long time too, haven’t you?

319
00:27:10,140 --> 00:27:12,460
That’s why you took him away from the palace.

320
00:27:15,932 --> 00:27:16,933
That's right.

321
00:27:19,415 --> 00:27:21,380
I was trying to stop him.

322
00:27:23,060 --> 00:27:25,040
That’s why I got Phob out of the palace.

323
00:27:26,820 --> 00:27:28,060
But in the end,

324
00:27:29,564 --> 00:27:31,140
none of it made any difference.

325
00:27:35,954 --> 00:27:38,220
I used to think the same thing—

326
00:27:39,515 --> 00:27:43,620
that if those two hadn’t fallen in love,

327
00:27:44,087 --> 00:27:45,700
everything

328
00:27:46,160 --> 00:27:48,260
might have been easier.

329
00:27:49,684 --> 00:27:53,640
But as time went by,

330
00:27:54,863 --> 00:27:57,060
I stopped thinking that way.

331
00:28:00,020 --> 00:28:01,460
Do you know why, Nual?

332
00:28:02,842 --> 00:28:04,990
Because…

333
00:28:05,684 --> 00:28:07,100
life is short.

334
00:28:08,106 --> 00:28:12,101
Far too short for us

335
00:28:12,820 --> 00:28:15,580
to waste it deciding who should love whom,

336
00:28:15,732 --> 00:28:18,420
or trying to tell people

337
00:28:18,900 --> 00:28:21,340
who they should or shouldn’t be with.

338
00:28:25,994 --> 00:28:28,220
And the same goes for you, Nual.

339
00:28:28,740 --> 00:28:30,741
If those two ever

340
00:28:31,500 --> 00:28:33,690
find their way back to each other,

341
00:28:34,660 --> 00:28:36,660
let them.

342
00:28:37,220 --> 00:28:39,460
Let go and stay out of it.

343
00:28:39,983 --> 00:28:41,580
It’s their life.

344
00:28:42,468 --> 00:28:45,380
Let them choose for themselves.

345
00:28:47,946 --> 00:28:50,380
- But I'm scared--
- I know. I know.

346
00:28:50,490 --> 00:28:52,260
I know. I get it.

347
00:28:52,580 --> 00:28:54,860
I understand your fear.

348
00:28:55,146 --> 00:28:57,940
But don’t let your fear

349
00:28:58,394 --> 00:29:02,746
become a cage for those two.

350
00:29:29,916 --> 00:29:31,100
Did you see her?

351
00:29:32,247 --> 00:29:34,420
She looked so tired and weak.

352
00:29:37,740 --> 00:29:39,860
I never wanted her to suffer.

353
00:29:42,226 --> 00:29:43,980
I never wanted any of this to happen.

354
00:29:45,842 --> 00:29:47,460
I feel guilty for what I’ve put you all through.

355
00:29:49,962 --> 00:29:53,700
From now on, try to visit her more often.

356
00:29:54,655 --> 00:29:58,100
And if there’s anything we can do for her,

357
00:29:59,194 --> 00:30:00,260
let’s do what we can.

358
00:30:01,402 --> 00:30:02,403
Sure, Mom.

359
00:30:17,260 --> 00:30:19,040
Take care of yourself too.

360
00:30:22,751 --> 00:30:23,940
You’ve lost so much weight, my dear.

361
00:31:13,644 --> 00:31:14,645
Dad.

362
00:31:20,618 --> 00:31:22,340
When did you come back?

363
00:31:23,160 --> 00:31:24,300
I just arrived this morning.

364
00:31:25,540 --> 00:31:27,395
I have some business to take care of in the capital.

365
00:31:29,336 --> 00:31:31,060
But I probably won’t be staying at home.

366
00:31:31,794 --> 00:31:33,140
I have quite a few things to do,

367
00:31:33,927 --> 00:31:35,540
so it’ll be more convenient for me to stay with Adul.

368
00:31:36,348 --> 00:31:38,020
Where is Chat?

369
00:31:39,495 --> 00:31:40,660
He's still in Nakhon Ratchasima.

370
00:31:41,727 --> 00:31:43,640
There're a lot for us to take care of.

371
00:31:48,634 --> 00:31:50,380
I heard that you were sick.

372
00:31:51,060 --> 00:31:52,061
How are you feeling?

373
00:31:52,228 --> 00:31:55,100
- Her health--
- I went to see the doctor already.

374
00:31:55,476 --> 00:31:59,100
The doctor gave me some medicine.

375
00:31:59,364 --> 00:32:00,940
I’ll be better in no time. I’m fine, dear.

376
00:32:03,607 --> 00:32:04,620
I will be fine.

377
00:32:10,599 --> 00:32:12,060
You’ve lost so much weight.

378
00:32:14,236 --> 00:32:15,500
Things must have been really hard for you.

379
00:32:16,988 --> 00:32:18,420
It hasn’t been easy,

380
00:32:19,394 --> 00:32:20,820
but I’m getting by.

381
00:32:22,394 --> 00:32:23,420
Hang in there, Tin.

382
00:32:24,564 --> 00:32:27,300
It won’t be long before everything goes back to the way it was.

383
00:32:29,412 --> 00:32:31,100
What do you mean?

384
00:32:32,660 --> 00:32:34,100
You’ll know when the time comes.

385
00:32:49,642 --> 00:32:52,620
We have submitted an application to register a political association

386
00:32:52,890 --> 00:32:54,740
under the name 'Free Siam Movement.'

387
00:32:55,172 --> 00:32:57,820
Our guiding principles are

388
00:32:58,090 --> 00:32:59,820
to uphold democracy

389
00:33:00,079 --> 00:33:03,900
and to preserve, for all time, the constitutional monarchy

390
00:33:04,012 --> 00:33:06,580
with the King as Head of State.

391
00:33:08,999 --> 00:33:11,700
Is this application to establish a political association

392
00:33:11,820 --> 00:33:14,540
intended to rival the Khana Ratsadon Association?

393
00:33:16,639 --> 00:33:19,541
We believe that our country has now become an oligarchy,

394
00:33:19,834 --> 00:33:22,602
ruled by a small group that seized power.

395
00:33:22,884 --> 00:33:25,820
The people have yet to enjoy true freedom,

396
00:33:26,383 --> 00:33:28,780
and this is a danger we must guard against.

397
00:33:29,044 --> 00:33:32,300
We therefore call upon all citizens to join us.

398
00:33:32,751 --> 00:33:36,140
Do you think people will join your group?

399
00:33:39,020 --> 00:33:40,021
[Free Siam Movement Launched]

400
00:33:40,040 --> 00:33:42,041
[Vows to Revive the Economy, Safeguard Independence, and Uphold the Constitution]

401
00:33:42,060 --> 00:33:43,561
[Unveils Its Principles to the Public for the First Time]

402
00:33:46,322 --> 00:33:49,540
It looks like Prince Vasin is serious this time.

403
00:33:51,260 --> 00:33:54,340
If this were just about forming a political association,

404
00:33:55,135 --> 00:33:57,540
I wouldn’t be this concerned.

405
00:33:58,522 --> 00:34:00,040
Our sources report unusual activity in Nakhon Ratchasima.

406
00:34:00,991 --> 00:34:01,992
Activities?

407
00:34:02,940 --> 00:34:03,941
How?

408
00:34:04,556 --> 00:34:07,060
They’ve been contacting several military units,

409
00:34:07,436 --> 00:34:10,420
holding secret meetings, and rallying supporters.

410
00:34:10,786 --> 00:34:12,580
We’re keeping a close watch to see

411
00:34:12,994 --> 00:34:14,540
which factions are joining them.

412
00:34:16,210 --> 00:34:19,500
If that’s true, it could lead to an armed confrontation.

413
00:34:23,863 --> 00:34:25,220
I don’t want that to happen.

414
00:34:25,646 --> 00:34:27,180
We’ve spent years talking about democracy

415
00:34:27,476 --> 00:34:28,900
and the future of our country.

416
00:34:29,968 --> 00:34:30,969
If, in the end,

417
00:34:31,908 --> 00:34:33,740
it all has to be decided by bullets,

418
00:34:36,657 --> 00:34:37,820
that would be a tragedy.

419
00:34:59,797 --> 00:35:00,980
How is it?

420
00:35:01,747 --> 00:35:05,260
Very good. With a few minor revisions, it should be ready for publication.

421
00:35:05,838 --> 00:35:07,980
- Really?
- Yes.

422
00:35:08,531 --> 00:35:09,980
I’ll see if I can find the right opportunity

423
00:35:10,000 --> 00:35:12,601
to publish it as a serial in the magazine.

424
00:35:13,804 --> 00:35:17,220
You're so talented and you should be proud of yourself.

425
00:35:19,868 --> 00:35:23,020
I want my father to be proud of me.

426
00:35:23,972 --> 00:35:27,866
I want him to see that what I’m doing has value.

427
00:35:28,319 --> 00:35:29,980
It may take some time.

428
00:35:31,386 --> 00:35:33,060
Your father’s generation

429
00:35:33,396 --> 00:35:35,900
isn’t used to seeing women pursue careers of their own.

430
00:35:36,620 --> 00:35:40,380
But one day, he’ll see just how capable you are.

431
00:35:44,940 --> 00:35:49,140
The Free Siam Movement held a public gathering in the capital,

432
00:35:49,402 --> 00:35:52,900
where Prince Vasin delivered a speech.

433
00:36:03,050 --> 00:36:07,580
Are you concerned about the Free Siam Movement?

434
00:36:08,452 --> 00:36:10,860
I’ve been hearing so much about them lately.

435
00:36:13,164 --> 00:36:15,620
Until now, we’ve been fortunate enough to avoid bloodshed.

436
00:36:16,636 --> 00:36:18,660
But if force is used this time,

437
00:36:20,940 --> 00:36:22,341
I fear it may end very differently.

438
00:36:22,594 --> 00:36:23,740
Is it really that serious?

439
00:36:26,500 --> 00:36:29,540
I don’t know much about politics,

440
00:36:30,060 --> 00:36:31,940
but I don’t want anyone to die.

441
00:36:34,356 --> 00:36:35,900
We’re all from the same country, after all.

442
00:36:48,620 --> 00:36:49,621
[Free Siam Movement Launched]

443
00:36:49,640 --> 00:36:51,641
[Vows to Revive the Economy, Safeguard Independence, and Uphold the Constitution]

444
00:36:58,314 --> 00:36:59,315
Dad?

445
00:37:01,007 --> 00:37:02,008
Where is your grandma?

446
00:37:02,996 --> 00:37:05,860
She went to the hospital with Aum, she will be back soon.

447
00:37:12,335 --> 00:37:14,260
I saw the news about the Free Siam Movement.

448
00:37:20,676 --> 00:37:23,060
I’m going to fight to reclaim Siam from them.

449
00:37:23,898 --> 00:37:26,860
They need to know that not everyone in Siam will bow to them.

450
00:37:28,202 --> 00:37:29,780
I don’t want you to do this.

451
00:37:30,897 --> 00:37:32,220
I have a bad feeling about it.

452
00:37:33,788 --> 00:37:34,860
Don't worry about me.

453
00:37:35,607 --> 00:37:38,420
Chat and I didn't do this alone.

454
00:37:38,817 --> 00:37:40,040
We still have the support

455
00:37:40,186 --> 00:37:42,660
of many members of the royal family.

456
00:37:43,340 --> 00:37:45,780
I don’t want any unrest.

457
00:37:46,100 --> 00:37:47,840
I just want our country to be at peace.

458
00:37:47,901 --> 00:37:49,300
They’re the ones who caused all this turmoil.

459
00:37:51,020 --> 00:37:52,221
They’re hungry for power,

460
00:37:53,021 --> 00:37:54,700
and they’ve torn apart the order of this country.

461
00:37:55,002 --> 00:37:57,300
We cannot stand by and let our nation continue like this.

462
00:37:57,466 --> 00:38:00,580
Maybe what they’ve done isn’t really as bad as it seems, Dad.

463
00:38:02,298 --> 00:38:03,299
What did you just say?

464
00:38:04,175 --> 00:38:05,460
I used to think the same way you do.

465
00:38:06,611 --> 00:38:07,940
I was angry with them.

466
00:38:10,170 --> 00:38:13,060
I thought they had taken everything away from us.

467
00:38:14,319 --> 00:38:17,340
But now that I’ve actually lived outside the palace

468
00:38:18,506 --> 00:38:20,300
and seen how ordinary people live...

469
00:38:22,180 --> 00:38:23,580
Dad, some of my students

470
00:38:24,543 --> 00:38:25,620
are nearly twenty

471
00:38:26,345 --> 00:38:28,980
and still can’t read or write.

472
00:38:30,676 --> 00:38:33,300
Some families have only just been able to afford to send their children to school

473
00:38:33,586 --> 00:38:35,460
after several taxes were abolished.

474
00:38:38,439 --> 00:38:39,440
Is it because of him?

475
00:38:40,903 --> 00:38:42,340
He brainwashed you.

476
00:38:42,524 --> 00:38:45,125
- It has nothing to do with Phob--
- Of course it has!

477
00:38:46,978 --> 00:38:48,460
He's always been around.

478
00:38:49,524 --> 00:38:52,180
He hates me for keeping him away from you.

479
00:38:52,988 --> 00:38:54,860
That’s why he came back to destroy us,

480
00:38:55,844 --> 00:38:59,100
to destroy our honor and our family name.

481
00:38:59,959 --> 00:39:02,660
Phob has never acted for his own gain.

482
00:39:03,020 --> 00:39:04,021
He may have been wrong.

483
00:39:05,210 --> 00:39:06,780
He may have made mistakes.

484
00:39:08,020 --> 00:39:09,821
But one thing I’m certain of is that

485
00:39:09,850 --> 00:39:12,540
he has never meant any harm to our country.

486
00:39:12,580 --> 00:39:13,860
You’re defending him?

487
00:39:16,953 --> 00:39:19,980
After everything he’s done to you? He used you.

488
00:39:21,492 --> 00:39:23,940
He used your love for him as a weapon.

489
00:39:23,993 --> 00:39:25,100
He destroyed our family.

490
00:39:25,599 --> 00:39:28,140
And after all that, you still love him?

491
00:39:37,641 --> 00:39:38,642
Fine.

492
00:39:39,860 --> 00:39:42,061
No matter how much you still love him,

493
00:39:42,668 --> 00:39:44,660
you can’t stop me from fighting for what I believe in.

494
00:39:45,927 --> 00:39:47,421
And I’m not alone anymore.

495
00:39:48,700 --> 00:39:52,220
Forces from several provinces are gathering as we speak.

496
00:39:52,663 --> 00:39:55,740
Those who love this country are preparing to rise and fight.

497
00:39:56,407 --> 00:39:59,540
Before long, everything will be the way it was again.

498
00:40:01,287 --> 00:40:02,620
What are you going to do?

499
00:40:25,556 --> 00:40:26,557
Phob.

500
00:40:27,402 --> 00:40:28,403
Have a seat.

501
00:40:29,439 --> 00:40:30,440
Yes, Your Highness.

502
00:40:36,655 --> 00:40:38,740
Why did you

503
00:40:39,540 --> 00:40:41,140
suddenly ask me to meet you out here?

504
00:40:41,652 --> 00:40:43,860
It’s dangerous for you to come out alone like this.

505
00:40:44,591 --> 00:40:46,220
Oh, I’m fine.

506
00:40:46,511 --> 00:40:48,980
I can still get around on my own.

507
00:40:49,247 --> 00:40:53,420
You’re acting as if I’m going to drop dead any day now.

508
00:40:56,250 --> 00:41:00,260
You know about Vasin's plan, don't you?

509
00:41:03,234 --> 00:41:04,235
I know about it.

510
00:41:06,306 --> 00:41:10,780
How are things in the country now?

511
00:41:11,319 --> 00:41:12,700
Is the situation serious?

512
00:41:17,105 --> 00:41:18,460
I’ve received word

513
00:41:19,591 --> 00:41:21,640
that the situation is very concerning, Your Highness.

514
00:41:22,300 --> 00:41:24,860
Troops are being mobilized, alliances are being formed,

515
00:41:25,287 --> 00:41:26,640
and several factions have begun making preparations.

516
00:41:27,681 --> 00:41:28,682
If we can’t stop this in time,

517
00:41:29,852 --> 00:41:31,225
there could be an armed confrontation.

518
00:41:31,500 --> 00:41:32,601
Oh my goodness.

519
00:41:33,951 --> 00:41:36,143
It is that serious?

520
00:41:38,804 --> 00:41:39,805
That's right.

521
00:41:40,650 --> 00:41:41,701
I didn't expect

522
00:41:43,418 --> 00:41:45,820
any of this to happen.

523
00:41:46,580 --> 00:41:49,581
We can't be so sure anymore.

524
00:41:55,226 --> 00:41:56,660
- Your Highness.
- Phob.

525
00:41:58,159 --> 00:42:00,180
If that day really comes,

526
00:42:00,954 --> 00:42:03,540
there’s something I want to ask of you.

527
00:42:04,350 --> 00:42:05,380
What is it?

528
00:42:08,199 --> 00:42:12,840
Please, don’t be too harsh on Vasin or Chat.

529
00:42:13,423 --> 00:42:15,500
I know,

530
00:42:15,887 --> 00:42:19,460
I understand that you’re on opposing sides.

531
00:42:22,671 --> 00:42:24,260
But whatever happens,

532
00:42:25,640 --> 00:42:27,140
Vasin is still my son,

533
00:42:27,999 --> 00:42:30,141
and Chat is still my grandson.

534
00:42:37,980 --> 00:42:39,300
You needn’t even ask, Your Highness.

535
00:42:41,410 --> 00:42:43,540
I would never harm Prince Vasin or

536
00:42:43,611 --> 00:42:44,860
Prince Chat.

537
00:42:47,975 --> 00:42:50,100
Thank you so much.

538
00:42:52,572 --> 00:42:58,340
Vasin and Tinakorn had an argument yesterday,

539
00:43:00,573 --> 00:43:02,860
over the very thing we’re talking about now.

540
00:43:05,930 --> 00:43:08,620
What did Prince Tinnakorn say?

541
00:43:09,404 --> 00:43:13,340
Tin said that not everything you’ve done

542
00:43:14,268 --> 00:43:16,940
is necessarily wrong.

543
00:43:17,857 --> 00:43:19,780
He knows you care about this country.

544
00:43:21,138 --> 00:43:24,220
You’re simply doing what you believe is right.

545
00:43:32,521 --> 00:43:33,540
Even after everything that’s happened,

546
00:43:35,370 --> 00:43:36,820
he still defends me.

547
00:43:39,738 --> 00:43:40,780
And yet I’m the one

548
00:43:42,255 --> 00:43:43,381
who hurt him,

549
00:43:44,940 --> 00:43:46,260
who caused him so much pain.

550
00:43:49,375 --> 00:43:50,580
I don’t deserve

551
00:43:51,839 --> 00:43:53,860
the kindness he’s shown me.

552
00:43:57,479 --> 00:44:01,780
I’ve watched the two of you grow up together.

553
00:44:02,700 --> 00:44:06,460
I know just

554
00:44:06,663 --> 00:44:08,740
how much you mean to each other.

555
00:44:11,356 --> 00:44:13,140
But I destroyed that bond

556
00:44:14,642 --> 00:44:16,020
with my own hands.

557
00:44:16,643 --> 00:44:19,644
But the bond between you isn’t completely broken, is it?

558
00:44:23,615 --> 00:44:26,380
Phob, listen to me.

559
00:44:27,364 --> 00:44:30,260
If one day the two of you

560
00:44:30,756 --> 00:44:33,300
find your way back to each other,

561
00:44:35,284 --> 00:44:38,060
hold on to each other tightly, just like this.

562
00:44:38,759 --> 00:44:40,604
Don’t let go

563
00:44:41,297 --> 00:44:43,479
because of the pain of the past.

564
00:44:44,577 --> 00:44:45,578
Okay?

565
00:44:48,100 --> 00:44:49,101
Yes, Your Highness.

566
00:45:31,140 --> 00:45:32,141
Your Highness!

567
00:45:36,640 --> 00:45:38,980
Your Highness! Your Highness!

568
00:45:41,107 --> 00:45:42,980
Your Highness! Your Highness!

569
00:45:43,535 --> 00:45:45,260
Your Highness! Your Highness!

570
00:45:46,009 --> 00:45:47,420
Your Highness! Your Highness!

571
00:45:48,820 --> 00:45:50,221
[Emergency Room]

572
00:46:00,500 --> 00:46:01,501
Phon?

573
00:46:02,873 --> 00:46:04,100
How is my grandma?

574
00:46:05,020 --> 00:46:06,380
The doctor is still checking on her.

575
00:46:06,820 --> 00:46:07,821
He hasn't come out with the update yet.

576
00:46:12,015 --> 00:46:15,240
What happened to my mom? What did you do to her?

577
00:46:15,711 --> 00:46:16,712
Dad!

578
00:46:17,311 --> 00:46:18,980
Are you her family? Come with me.

579
00:46:24,559 --> 00:46:25,560
You should go.

580
00:46:26,906 --> 00:46:27,907
Please leave.

581
00:46:59,178 --> 00:47:00,179
Grandma.

582
00:47:01,450 --> 00:47:02,780
How is my mother?

583
00:47:03,290 --> 00:47:06,420
Her kidney condition has worsened considerably.

584
00:47:06,820 --> 00:47:08,821
She has been very weak for some time,

585
00:47:09,071 --> 00:47:12,040
and this fall has made her condition even worse.

586
00:47:17,420 --> 00:47:18,421
Is there any way to treat her?

587
00:47:18,858 --> 00:47:22,100
Her kidneys are barely functioning now.

588
00:47:22,431 --> 00:47:24,700
Waste is building up in her blood,

589
00:47:24,911 --> 00:47:27,260
and her body is growing weaker by the day.

590
00:47:27,416 --> 00:47:28,620
As her kidneys fail,

591
00:47:28,988 --> 00:47:32,500
her other organs will gradually be affected as well.

592
00:47:33,180 --> 00:47:36,180
At this point, all we can do is provide supportive care

593
00:47:36,551 --> 00:47:40,060
and keep her as comfortable as possible.

594
00:48:07,186 --> 00:48:09,220
What did you do to my mom?

595
00:48:10,284 --> 00:48:11,285
I didn't do anything.

596
00:48:11,410 --> 00:48:12,580
Liar!

597
00:48:13,311 --> 00:48:16,140
My mom went to see you, and she came back like this?!

598
00:48:18,159 --> 00:48:20,460
- It was an accident.
- An accident?

599
00:48:22,040 --> 00:48:23,340
How dare you say that to me?

600
00:48:24,247 --> 00:48:27,940
Haven’t you taken enough from me already?

601
00:48:29,362 --> 00:48:30,780
You took my son.

602
00:48:31,479 --> 00:48:34,181
You took my family’s trust.

603
00:48:34,511 --> 00:48:35,900
You took my palace,

604
00:48:36,500 --> 00:48:39,190
the honor of my royal house—everything!

605
00:48:40,463 --> 00:48:43,040
And now you’re going to take my mother from me too?!

606
00:48:43,702 --> 00:48:44,703
Huh?

607
00:48:47,553 --> 00:48:48,554
I'm sorry.

608
00:48:49,574 --> 00:48:50,575
You're sorry?

609
00:48:54,151 --> 00:48:57,420
The doctor said her kidneys have stopped working.

610
00:48:58,337 --> 00:49:01,100
Her other organs will start failing too.

611
00:49:03,138 --> 00:49:04,860
He told us to prepare for the worst.

612
00:50:17,810 --> 00:50:19,040
I’ve already contacted Chat.

613
00:50:21,040 --> 00:50:22,580
He’s coming back from Nakhon Ratchasima tomorrow.

614
00:50:23,890 --> 00:50:24,891
I’ll go meet him when he arrives.

615
00:50:26,508 --> 00:50:27,700
I'm glad he could come.

616
00:50:30,759 --> 00:50:32,140
Grandma must want to meet him.

617
00:50:44,922 --> 00:50:47,060
I'm sure Grandma will get better.

618
00:50:48,058 --> 00:50:49,700
She's a strong woman.

619
00:50:52,727 --> 00:50:53,728
It is because of him.

620
00:50:55,687 --> 00:50:58,640
If she hadn't gone out to meet him, it wouldn't have been like this.

621
00:50:59,538 --> 00:51:01,220
Dad, it was an accident.

622
00:51:03,143 --> 00:51:04,144
It was an accident.

623
00:51:06,578 --> 00:51:07,860
If we still had our palace,

624
00:51:08,572 --> 00:51:10,300
with money and everything,

625
00:51:11,500 --> 00:51:13,500
your grandma wouldn't have been like this.

626
00:51:17,388 --> 00:51:19,500
It is all because of Phob, that son of a bitch.

627
00:51:35,402 --> 00:51:37,343
Or maybe it's all because of me.

628
00:51:40,634 --> 00:51:41,660
The palace,

629
00:51:43,108 --> 00:51:44,640
our entire family line...

630
00:51:47,044 --> 00:51:49,180
it’s all going to come to an end with me.

631
00:51:53,588 --> 00:51:55,860
And now I'm about to lose my mom.

632
00:51:58,898 --> 00:52:00,500
There's nothing I can do.

633
00:52:04,799 --> 00:52:06,740
I’ve never been able to protect anyone.

634
00:52:53,394 --> 00:52:54,395
Aum.

635
00:52:59,031 --> 00:53:02,257
You should get some rest. I can stay here with her.

636
00:53:03,740 --> 00:53:05,340
Where is Prince Vasin?

637
00:53:06,260 --> 00:53:08,940
He went to pick up Chat at Hua Lamphong Station.

638
00:53:10,268 --> 00:53:11,269
They will follow us here.

639
00:53:30,236 --> 00:53:31,237
Grandma.

640
00:53:33,922 --> 00:53:35,708
Chat and Dad will be here soon.

641
00:53:38,154 --> 00:53:39,433
Please wait for them.

642
00:53:50,138 --> 00:53:52,380
Doctor! Doctor!

643
00:53:53,156 --> 00:53:54,500
Doctor! She's awake!

644
00:53:57,914 --> 00:53:58,915
Grandma.

645
00:53:59,860 --> 00:54:00,861
Grandma.

646
00:54:02,548 --> 00:54:03,549
Grandma.

647
00:54:04,969 --> 00:54:06,460
Grandma. Grandma.

648
00:54:06,900 --> 00:54:07,901
Tin, dear.

649
00:54:09,583 --> 00:54:11,460
- Tin.
- Grandma, I am right here.

650
00:54:13,449 --> 00:54:17,100
Such a crybaby, aren’t you?

651
00:54:18,042 --> 00:54:19,440
That's not true.

652
00:54:22,010 --> 00:54:24,207
You’re still a terrible liar.

653
00:54:26,380 --> 00:54:27,381
Grandma,

654
00:54:28,212 --> 00:54:30,140
please stay strong.

655
00:54:30,975 --> 00:54:32,100
The doctor is coming

656
00:54:32,671 --> 00:54:34,620
and we will go home.

657
00:54:38,844 --> 00:54:40,580
Please don't leave me.

658
00:54:41,132 --> 00:54:42,580
I have no one left.

659
00:54:43,953 --> 00:54:45,660
Who says you have no one left?

660
00:54:46,897 --> 00:54:48,460
Your father’s still here.

661
00:54:49,348 --> 00:54:51,060
So are Chat

662
00:54:52,188 --> 00:54:53,589
and Aum.

663
00:54:55,202 --> 00:54:58,603
And the person who loves you…

664
00:54:59,652 --> 00:55:01,200
is still here too.

665
00:55:02,196 --> 00:55:04,700
But I want you here with me.

666
00:55:06,063 --> 00:55:07,100
Tin, dear.

667
00:55:08,599 --> 00:55:10,040
Loss…

668
00:55:11,351 --> 00:55:12,631
is something

669
00:55:14,087 --> 00:55:17,575
none of us can escape.

670
00:55:18,420 --> 00:55:20,140
So while we still have each other,

671
00:55:21,068 --> 00:55:23,940
we should cherish every moment.

672
00:55:29,098 --> 00:55:30,099
Grandma.

673
00:55:30,458 --> 00:55:32,591
Promise me…

674
00:55:34,138 --> 00:55:35,850
you’ll be happy.

675
00:55:37,556 --> 00:55:39,500
That you won’t be alone,

676
00:55:41,407 --> 00:55:45,020
and you won’t close your heart off.

677
00:55:46,303 --> 00:55:48,220
Sure, I promise you.

678
00:55:54,383 --> 00:55:56,460
My good boy.

679
00:55:56,986 --> 00:55:57,987
Grandma.

680
00:56:01,103 --> 00:56:02,300
Grandma.

681
00:56:15,444 --> 00:56:16,445
Grandma.

682
00:56:17,660 --> 00:56:18,661
Grandma.

683
00:56:19,580 --> 00:56:20,581
Grandma.

684
00:56:27,844 --> 00:56:28,845
Grandma.

685
00:56:29,845 --> 00:56:31,700
Grandma, wake up!

686
00:56:33,224 --> 00:56:34,225
Grandma.

687
00:56:37,020 --> 00:56:39,580
Don't leave me alone!

688
00:57:13,223 --> 00:57:15,140
May the merit we have made

689
00:57:15,746 --> 00:57:17,938
be dedicated to Princess Patthamapriya.

690
00:57:18,962 --> 00:57:21,500
She was so good to me,

691
00:57:23,114 --> 00:57:26,820
yet I couldn’t even be there to pay my final respects.

692
00:57:43,244 --> 00:57:44,620
I’m sure she would understand.

693
00:57:45,356 --> 00:57:48,380
If we had gone, we would’ve only caused more trouble.

694
00:57:54,479 --> 00:57:55,580
I have no idea

695
00:57:57,524 --> 00:57:59,103
how Prince Vasin is holding up?

696
00:58:01,076 --> 00:58:02,077
What about Prince Chatthorn?

697
00:58:03,257 --> 00:58:04,500
And Prince Tinnakorn.

698
00:58:07,183 --> 00:58:09,260
I’m so worried about them, my dear.

699
00:58:39,548 --> 00:58:40,962
Why did this have to happen?

700
00:58:42,418 --> 00:58:43,860
If Grandma hadn’t gone to see Phob,

701
00:58:44,906 --> 00:58:45,980
none of this would’ve happened.

702
00:58:46,303 --> 00:58:47,304
Chat.

703
00:58:48,010 --> 00:58:50,436
It was an accident. Don’t you get it, it was a freaking accident.

704
00:58:54,228 --> 00:58:55,300
An accident?

705
00:58:57,322 --> 00:59:00,836
What good has Phop ever brought into our lives?

706
00:59:01,940 --> 00:59:03,300
We lost the palace,

707
00:59:04,186 --> 00:59:06,620
our positions, and now Grandmother too.

708
00:59:06,740 --> 00:59:08,260
- It has nothing to do--
- Enough!

709
00:59:15,956 --> 00:59:17,640
This isn’t the time to be arguing.

710
00:59:19,668 --> 00:59:22,047
We have far more important things to deal with right now.

711
00:59:24,740 --> 00:59:25,741
Tinnakorn,

712
00:59:27,354 --> 00:59:28,612
you’re coming with me to Nakhon Ratchasima

713
00:59:29,962 --> 00:59:31,530
Our troops are ready.

714
00:59:32,180 --> 00:59:34,560
Within days, they’ll be able to march on the capital and lay siege to it.

715
00:59:34,620 --> 00:59:35,621
Dad?

716
00:59:36,562 --> 00:59:38,236
We’ve come this far.

717
00:59:38,999 --> 00:59:40,188
There’s no turning back now.

718
00:59:41,840 --> 00:59:43,140
Please, don't do it.

719
00:59:44,418 --> 00:59:45,580
I'm worried about you.

720
00:59:47,002 --> 00:59:48,003
I'm worried about Chat.

721
00:59:51,188 --> 00:59:52,820
We’ve already lost Grandma.

722
00:59:54,780 --> 00:59:55,781
I can’t bear

723
00:59:56,353 --> 00:59:57,860
to lose anyone else.

724
00:59:58,591 --> 01:00:00,580
I’ve already lost my mother.

725
01:00:02,567 --> 01:00:06,220
This land is all I have left. I’ll never let those people take it from me.

726
01:00:08,700 --> 01:00:10,340
If we don’t rise up and fight now,

727
01:00:11,073 --> 01:00:14,420
our land will continue to be violated with no end in sight.

728
01:00:14,474 --> 01:00:17,900
But Dad, rising up and resorting to force

729
01:00:18,031 --> 01:00:19,807
won’t solve anything.

730
01:00:20,943 --> 01:00:23,544
We’re all from the same country. Why can’t we just talk this through nicely?

731
01:00:23,706 --> 01:00:25,140
When they seized power,

732
01:00:25,660 --> 01:00:27,340
did they ever try to reason with us?

733
01:00:30,340 --> 01:00:31,341
Hey,

734
01:00:31,775 --> 01:00:33,428
This is our chance.

735
01:00:34,356 --> 01:00:35,660
If we succeed,

736
01:00:36,372 --> 01:00:38,415
we might be able to get everything back.

737
01:00:39,423 --> 01:00:40,424
Chat?

738
01:00:41,071 --> 01:00:42,072
Tinnakorn.

739
01:00:43,977 --> 01:00:45,060
You have to choose now.

740
01:00:46,631 --> 01:00:49,298
Are you on my side or his?

741
01:00:59,583 --> 01:01:01,618
Please don't force me to pick side.

742
01:01:04,281 --> 01:01:05,282
Fine.

743
01:01:06,788 --> 01:01:08,431
It's okay if you can't choose.

744
01:01:09,919 --> 01:01:11,268
But I want you to know this:

745
01:01:12,360 --> 01:01:14,820
if I have to face Phob,

746
01:01:15,620 --> 01:01:17,180
I will not spare his life.

747
01:01:18,543 --> 01:01:19,544
Dad?

748
01:01:20,735 --> 01:01:24,380
Whether for personal reasons or our opposing beliefs,

749
01:01:25,188 --> 01:01:27,180
there is no way...

750
01:01:27,855 --> 01:01:30,292
Phob and I can live under the same sky.

751
01:01:56,700 --> 01:01:59,500
Those bastards will have no place in this land. Will you fight or not?

752
01:01:59,601 --> 01:02:01,190
We will fight!

753
01:02:04,740 --> 01:02:06,300
Can you promise me one thing?

754
01:02:08,154 --> 01:02:10,180
Promise me that you will come back to me.

